    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  A <span class=\"learn-keyword\">consignment</span> is an arrangement in which goods are sent by their owner to an agent in another location for the purpose of sale, while ownership of the goods remains with the sender until they are actually sold.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Parties Involved</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Party</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Consignor</td><td>The owner of the goods who sends them out for sale; remains the legal owner until sold</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Consignee</td><td>The agent who receives the goods and sells them on behalf of the consignor, in exchange for a commission</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Features of Consignment</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Ownership of goods remains with the consignor until sold by the consignee</li>\n  <li>The consignee acts as an agent, not a buyer, and is not liable for unsold goods</li>\n  <li>The consignee earns a commission on sales made, not a profit margin like an owner would</li>\n  <li>Any loss or profit on eventual sale belongs to the consignor, not the consignee</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Key Documents</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Document</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Proforma invoice</td><td>Sent by the consignor to the consignee listing the goods dispatched and their value; it is NOT a demand for payment, since the consignee has not bought the goods</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Account sales</td><td>Sent by the consignee to the consignor, showing goods sold, expenses incurred, commission earned, and the net amount due to the consignor</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Consignment vs. Sale</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Consignment</th><th>Sale</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Ownership remains with the consignor until sold</td><td>Ownership transfers to the buyer immediately</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Consignee is an agent</td><td>Buyer is an independent party</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Consignee bears no risk of loss on unsold goods</td><td>Buyer bears full risk once purchased</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Terms Used in Consignment</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Del credere commission</td><td>An extra commission paid to the consignee for taking on the risk of bad debts from credit sales</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Ordinary commission</td><td>The normal commission paid to the consignee for selling the goods</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Normal loss</td><td>An expected, unavoidable loss (e.g., evaporation, natural wastage) that is absorbed into the cost of remaining stock</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Abnormal loss</td><td>An unexpected loss (e.g., due to fire, theft, or accident) that is charged directly to the profit and loss account, not spread over remaining stock</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Never confuse a proforma invoice with a normal sales invoice — a proforma invoice does not create a debtor-creditor relationship because ownership has not transferred.\n</div>\n",
